.SH "NAME"
econf_hasQuotes \- check whether the value of a key is enclosed by quotes

.SH "SYNOPSIS"

.sp
.ft B
.nf
#include <libeconf\&.h>
.fi
.ft
.sp

.BI "bool econf_hasQuotes(econf_file\ *" "kf" ", const\ char\ *" "group" ", const\ char\ *" "key" ");"

.SH "DESCRIPTION"

.PP
The \fBeconf_hasQuotes\fR() function checks whether the value of the key specified by \fIgroup\fR and \fIkey\fR in the given configuration file object \fIkf\fR is enclosed by quotes\&. If \fIgroup\fR is \fBNULL\fR, the key is considered to belong to no group\&.

.PP
A value is enclosed by quotes either because it was parsed from a configuration file where it was written with a leading quote character, or because it was marked as such with \fBeconf_setQuotes\fR()\&. This flag only affects how the value will be enclosed by quotes when the configuration is written back with \fBeconf_writeFile\fR()\&.

.SH "RETURN VALUE"

.PP
\fBeconf_hasQuotes\fR()
returns
\fBtrue\fR
if the value of the given \fIgroup\fR/\fIkey\fR is enclosed by quotes, and
\fBfalse\fR
otherwise\&.

.PP
\fBfalse\fR
is also returned if
\fIkf\fR
is
\fBNULL\fR, or if the
\fIgroup\fR/\fIkey\fR
combination has not been found\&.

.SH "SEE ALSO"

.PP
\fBlibeconf\fR(3),
\fBeconf_setQuotes\fR(3),
\fBeconf_writeFile\fR(3)\&
